      "node_id": "IC_kwDOCsXIds8AAAABORObhg",
      "user": {
        "login": "jpantonow",
        "id": 129221613,
        "node_id": "U_kgDOB7PD7Q",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129221613?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jpantonow",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/following{/other_user}",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/gists{/gist_id}",
        "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
        "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/subscriptions",
        "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/orgs",
        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T11:30:21Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T11:30:21Z",
      "body": "> What is the reason for replacing MD5 here?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Probably because MD5 is cryptographically broken and insecure and AI cannot detect that it is used as a non-security related cache hash generation and thus perfectly fine.\r\n\r\nThe change came from a finding I got while running a dynamic security analysis on the app. During execution, the tool flagged this use of `MessageDigest.getInstance(\"MD5\")` as a `MessageDigestSpec` violation, since MD5 is not part of the accepted set of digest algorithms. That's why I proposed switching it to SHA-256. The intention wasn't to change how the cache works, but to address the issue reported by the analysis while keeping the same behavior. Since the hash is only used for derived cache entries, the main side effect should be that existing entries become cache misses and are regenerated.\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/SapuSeven/BetterUntis/issues/comments/5252553606/reactions",
