      "created_at": "2026-08-11T11:57:19Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T11:57:19Z",
      "body": "> While MD5 may not be supported on every jvm the android jvm is explicitly supporting MD5: https://developer.android.com/reference/java/security/MessageDigest\r\n\r\nYes, MD5 is supported by Android. The issue here isn't JVM compatibility, but the `MessageDigestSpec` used by the dynamic analysis tool, which flagged this MD5 call during execution because it considers MD5 an insecure digest. The change to SHA-256 was simply meant to address that finding while keeping the cache behavior unchanged.\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
