        "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SapuSeven/orgs",
        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SapuSeven/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SapuSeven/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SapuSeven/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T20:34:26Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T20:38:07Z",
      "body": "Ok this is not leading anywhere.\r\n\r\n@jpantonow I already stated that I will not be accepting AI generated PRs. I don't know if you used AI for this analysis because you didn't even mention the name of this tool, but there are strong indications of it.\r\n\r\nAs @lm41 mentioned, there is no need for a cryptographically secure hashing algorithm since it's only used to generate random cache file names.\r\nMD5 works and is the simplest way to accomplish that.\r\n\r\nSince there doesn't seem to be a reason for this change other than a finding from some unknown analysis tool and there are no security or stability implications, I'll be closing this PR.",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
